## Console Lockdown
## https://forums.whonix.org/t/etc-security-hardening/8592

## This is the error message should this fail:
## sudo su
## sudo: PAM account management error: Permission denied

## see also:
## man access.conf
## man pam_access

## Usually tty7 is for X.
## Qubes uses tty1 for X.

## Qubes has 'pts/0' when for example running "sudo" from a terminal emulator.
## Qubes uses 'hvc0' when using in dom0 "sudo xl console vm-name".
## When using systemd-nspawn (chroot) then `login` requires console 'console' to be permitted.

## Allow members of group `console` to use:
## - 'console'
## - 'tty1' to 'tty7'
## - 'pts/0' to 'pts/9'
## - 'hvc0' to 'hvc9'
## serial console
## https://forums.whonix.org/t/how-do-i-enter-the-whonix-shell-from-cli/7271/43
## - 'ttyS0' to 'ttyS9'
## - 'login'
## A login-service session with no tty (VBoxService guest control, which
## chains to the 'login' PAM service) presents origin 'login', not a tty, so
## it matches none of the tty entries above and would hit the catch-all deny
## below. Permitting 'login' means membership in group 'console' is enough to
## allow guest control, without needing 'console-unrestricted' (which stays
## the full-unrestriction escape hatch). Guest control already requires host
## control of the VM, so this does not widen the trust boundary.
## pam_access matches an origin token against PAM_RHOST as well as the tty,
## so 'login' would also match a remote host named 'login'. DNS resolution of
## origin tokens is disabled (nodns, set on the pam_access line in the
## console-lockdown-security-misc pam-config), so a resolvable 'login.<domain>'
## cannot match; the only residual is a literal PAM_RHOST=login, which no
## default service produces for the 'login' service (sshd uses its own service;
## login(1) sets PAM_RHOST only under telnetd/rlogind, which are not installed).
+:(console):console tty1 tty2 tty3 tty4 tty5 tty6 tty7 pts/0 pts/1 pts/2 pts/3 pts/4 pts/5 pts/6 pts/7 pts/8 pts/9 hvc0 hvc1 hvc2 hvc3 hvc4 hvc5 hvc6 hvc7 hvc8 hvc9 ttyS0 ttyS1 ttyS2 ttyS3 ttyS4 ttyS5 ttyS6 ttyS7 ttyS8 ttyS9 login

## Same as above also for members of group `sudo`.
## https://github.com/Kicksecure/security-misc/pull/74#issuecomment-607748407
+:(sudo):console tty1 tty2 tty3 tty4 tty5 tty6 tty7 pts/0 pts/1 pts/2 pts/3 pts/4 pts/5 pts/6 pts/7 pts/8 pts/9 hvc0 hvc1 hvc2 hvc3 hvc4 hvc5 hvc6 hvc7 hvc8 hvc9 ttyS0 ttyS1 ttyS2 ttyS3 ttyS4 ttyS5 ttyS6 ttyS7 ttyS8 ttyS9 login

## Everyone else except members of group 'console-unrestricted'
## are restricted from everything else.
-:ALL EXCEPT (console-unrestricted):ALL
